      <section class="wrap section" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
        <header class="section-heading">
          <p class="label">Current research</p>
          <h2 id="research-title">Pretraining &amp; control</h2>
        </header>
        <div class="research-content">
          <article class="current-role">
            <p class="status">Current affiliation</p>
            <h3>Galaxea AI</h3>
            <p class="role">
              Pretraining Team &middot; Advised by <a href="https://iiis.tsinghua.edu.cn/en/People/Faculty/ZhaoHang.htm">Prof. Hang Zhao</a> (Tsinghua
              University)
            </p>
            <p>I contribute to an upcoming world action model and the team&rsquo;s next-generation embodied foundation model.</p>
            <p class="data-contribution">
              <strong>Pretraining data.</strong> I&rsquo;m responsible for key parts of the robot data pipeline, including data processing algorithms
              and database management. My work earned high performance ratings for three consecutive months.
            </p>
          </article>
          <div class="research-topics">
            <article class="topic">
              <p class="label">Work in progress</p>
              <h3>VLA Pretraining Dynamics</h3>
              <p>I study when useful robot capabilities emerge during pretraining and how data and training choices shape what a policy learns.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="topic">
              <p class="label">Work in progress</p>
              <h3>Robot-Use Agents &amp; Dual Systems</h3>
              <p>I explore dual-system architectures that pair high-level agent planning with low-level robot policies for physical execution.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="work-band">
        <section class="wrap section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
          <header class="section-heading">
            <p class="label">Publication</p>
            <h2 id="work-title">Selected work</h2>
          </header>
          <article class="paper">
            <p class="status">RSS 2026 &middot; RoboData Workshop</p>
            <h3>
              <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.08520"
                >Two Bridges, One Pathway: From VLMs to Generalizable VLAs with Embodied Trajectory-Coupled Data</a
              >
            </h3>
            <p class="authors">
              Linqi Yin*, Shiduo Zhang*, <strong>Shenling Qiu*</strong>, Chenxin Li, Zhaoyang Fu, Lei Xiao, Xiang Wang, Chenchen Yang, Zhe Xu,
              Pengfang Qian, Jingjing Gong, Xipeng Qiu, Xuanjing Huang, Yu-Gang Jiang
            </p>
            <p class="note">* Equal contribution</p>
            <p>
              We use supervision derived from robot trajectories to bridge the input and training-objective gaps between vision-language models and
              robot policies.
            </p>
            <a class="paper-link" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.08520">Read on arXiv</a>
          </article>
        </section>
      </div>

